### IntelliJ HTTP Client. Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html

GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks?priority=HIGH&done=false

### 404 as ProblemDetail
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/99

### Create. Try sending "id" or "done" too: they are ignored (that is what the DTO is for)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Write docs", "description": "README and Swagger", "priority": "LOW", "dueDate": "2030-01-01"}

### Validation: expect 400 with an errors map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "", "dueDate": "2020-01-01"}

### Duplicate title: expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "learn spring", "priority": "LOW"}

### Malformed JSON: expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{bad

### Replace
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Learn Spring Boot", "priority": "HIGH", "done": true}

###
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/2/complete

###
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/3

### Negative id: expect 400
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/-1
